From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Luau and Android fixes: multiplayer only when started from its screen, Escape closes it

- global.lua: no goto (Luau), setMapMarkers goes through addAction with a name
- menu.lua: panel centred in GUI units (ui.screenSize is pixels), Escape closes it, 'Active' is set only by the
  screen's New/Load and cleared on startup, on returning to the menu and on the main menu's own New/Load
- global.lua only connects, hosts or retries after the player script's 'configure' (a plain game stays silent)
- player.lua / trade.lua: UI in GUI units; the player script stays dormant unless 'Active'
- main menu: New/Load clicks are reported to menu scripts

---
diff --git a/apps/openmw/mwgui/mainmenu.cpp b/apps/openmw/mwgui/mainmenu.cpp
--- a/apps/openmw/mwgui/mainmenu.cpp
+++ b/apps/openmw/mwgui/mainmenu.cpp
@@ -171,6 +171,9 @@
 
         const std::string& name = *sender->getUserData<std::string>();
         winMgr->playSound(ESM::RefId::stringRefId("Menu Click"));
+        // Menu scripts hear about every start of a game from the main menu (the multiplayer mod drops its session)
+        if (name == "newgame" || name == "loadgame")
+            MWBase::Environment::get().getLuaManager()->mainMenuButton(name);
         if (name == "return")
             winMgr->removeGuiMode(GM_MainMenu);
         else if (name == "multiplayer")
